Backport of llvm/llvm-project PR #173002 (fix for issue #154714).

ProgramStack.cpp calls malloc/free in the LLVM_HAS_SPLIT_STACKS branch of
runOnNewStack without including <cstdlib>; the declarations only ever
arrived transitively through other LLVM and libc++ headers. The Xcode 26
toolchain's libc++ no longer includes <cstdlib> transitively, so the file
stops compiling on macOS:

    error: use of undeclared identifier 'malloc'
    error: use of undeclared identifier 'free'

Applies to LLVM 21.1.8; upstream fixed it on main via #173002.

--- a/llvm/lib/Support/ProgramStack.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Support/ProgramStack.cpp
@@ -18,9 +18,10 @@
 # include <intrin.h>  // for _AddressOfReturnAddress
 #endif
 
 #ifndef LLVM_HAS_SPLIT_STACKS
 # include "llvm/Support/thread.h"
 #endif
+#include <cstdlib> // malloc/free in runOnNewStack (upstream llvm/llvm-project#173002)
 
 using namespace llvm;
 
